<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Glauchau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Glauchau is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwickauer-mulde">Zwickauer Mulde</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From the late 12th century it was the main seat of the Schönburg family, whose two castles, Forderglauchau and Hinterglauchau, still stand there. In the 19th century it became an important centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> textile industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/glauchau.jpg" alt="Glauchau" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Sander · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Markt_Glauchau.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
